TASK SPECIFICATIONS:
{
  "id": "SELF002",
  "title": "Reversing jog drive with a neutral scan",
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "requirements": "# SELF002: Bidirectional Reversing Interlock with One-Scan Stop\n\n## Background\nForward/reverse motor interlock preventing immediate reversal on consecutive scans.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n1. Inputs: `ForwardButton`, `ReverseButton`, and `Stop` (`BOOL`).\n2. Compute desired direction: `0` (stop) if `Stop = TRUE` or `ForwardButton = ReverseButton`; `+1` if only `ForwardButton = TRUE`; `-1` if only `ReverseButton = TRUE`.\n3. If desired direction is nonzero and opposite to the previous scan's active direction (`-1` vs `+1`), force both outputs FALSE for this one intermediate stop scan (clearing direction memory to `0`).\n4. Otherwise output the desired direction (`Forward := (dir = +1)`, `Reverse := (dir = -1)`) and store it.\n\n## Interface\n- **Inputs:** `ForwardButton: BOOL`, `ReverseButton: BOOL`, `Stop: BOOL`\n- **Outputs:** `Forward: BOOL`, `Reverse: BOOL`\n\n## Initial Values\n- `previous_direction=0`, `Forward=false`, `Reverse=false`\n\n## Timing & Evaluation Conventions\nAll inputs are level-sensitive; direction memory initializes to `0` (stopped).",
  "scenario": "A reversible positioning drive must break its previous direction command for one full output scan before reversing.",
  "interface": [
    {
      "direction": "INPUT",
      "name": "ForwardButton",
      "type": "BOOL",
      "description": "Forward jog request"
    },
    {
      "direction": "INPUT",
      "name": "ReverseButton",
      "type": "BOOL",
      "description": "Reverse jog request"
    },
    {
      "direction": "INPUT",
      "name": "Stop",
      "type": "BOOL",
      "description": "Stop request"
    },
    {
      "direction": "OUTPUT",
      "name": "Forward",
      "type": "BOOL",
      "description": "Forward contactor command"
    },
    {
      "direction": "OUTPUT",
      "name": "Reverse",
      "type": "BOOL",
      "description": "Reverse contactor command"
    }
  ],
  "initial_conditions": {
    "previous_direction": 0,
    "Forward": false,
    "Reverse": false
  },
  "scan_semantics": "At scan k, sample every input once, read retained pre-state q[k], execute one transition, and observe outputs O[k] at the end of that same scan. Updated state becomes q[k+1]. Reset the instance before each test. Step 0 executes normally; initial conditions describe pre-state, not an extra delayed scan. All timing in this task is explicitly counted in invocations, not wall time.",
  "safety_priority": [
    "Stop and ambiguous button combinations command neutral",
    "Opposite-direction request inserts neutral"
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The task interface, requirements, assumptions, and normalized LTL definitions (excluding reference-only ground truth) are supplied identically to both frameworks. Output names always denote observed candidate outputs, never precomputed expected values.",
    "The task interface, requirements, assumptions, and normalized LTL definitions (excluding reference-only ground truth) are supplied identically to both frameworks. Output names always denote observed candidate outputs, never precomputed expected values."
  ],
  "atomic_propositions": {
    "ForwardButton": "I[k].ForwardButton: sampled input (BOOL).",
    "ReverseButton": "I[k].ReverseButton: sampled input (BOOL).",
    "Stop": "I[k].Stop: sampled input (BOOL).",
    "Forward": "O[k].Forward: independently observed post-scan candidate value (BOOL); never defined as expected output.",
    "Reverse": "O[k].Reverse: independently observed post-scan candidate value (BOOL); never defined as expected output.",
    "first": "k=0; first invocation, not the pre-invocation observation",
    "qForward": "{\"kind\": \"previous_observed_output\", \"source\": \"O[k-1].Forward\", \"initial\": false, \"update\": \"After comparing scan k, store ACTUAL O[k].Forward; never write into reference state.\"}",
    "qReverse": "{\"kind\": \"previous_observed_output\", \"source\": \"O[k-1].Reverse\", \"initial\": false, \"update\": \"After comparing scan k, store ACTUAL O[k].Reverse; never write into reference state.\"}",
    "fwdOnly": "ForwardButton & !ReverseButton & !Stop.",
    "revOnly": "ReverseButton & !ForwardButton & !Stop.",
    "init": "At the separate pre-invocation initial observation before scan k=0: O_init.Forward=false, O_init.Reverse=false."
  },
  "ltl": [
    {
      "id": "SELF002.P_init",
      "kind": "safety",
      "formula": "init",
      "description": "Before the first scan invocation, all declared OUTPUT variables and initial instance state hold their declared initial values.",
      "explanation": "Applies strictly to the fresh pre-invocation initial instance observation before scan k=0 (INITIAL_INSTANCE scope).",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "INITIAL_INSTANCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "SELF002.P1",
      "formula": "G(!(Forward & Reverse))",
      "explanation": "Direction outputs are mutually exclusive.",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "SCAN_SEQUENCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "SELF002.P2",
      "formula": "G((Stop | (ForwardButton <-> ReverseButton)) -> (!Forward & !Reverse))",
      "explanation": "Invalid or stopped requests produce neutral.",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "SCAN_SEQUENCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "SELF002.P3",
      "formula": "G((fwdOnly & qReverse) -> (!Forward & !Reverse))",
      "explanation": "Reversal from reverse has one neutral output scan.",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "SCAN_SEQUENCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "SELF002.P4",
      "formula": "G((revOnly & qForward) -> (!Forward & !Reverse))",
      "explanation": "Reversal from forward has one neutral output scan.",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "SCAN_SEQUENCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "SELF002.P5",
      "formula": "G((fwdOnly & !qReverse) -> Forward)",
      "explanation": "A permitted forward jog operates immediately.",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "SCAN_SEQUENCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "SELF002.P6",
      "formula": "G((revOnly & !qForward) -> Reverse)",
      "explanation": "A permitted reverse jog operates immediately.",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "SCAN_SEQUENCE"
    }
  ]
}

ARCHITECTURAL PLAN:
{
  "state_machine": {
    "states": [
      {
        "name": "STOPPED",
        "meaning": "previous_direction=0; outputs neutral; also the one-scan neutral result for an opposite-direction request"
      },
      {
        "name": "FORWARD",
        "meaning": "previous_direction=+1; Forward commanded"
      },
      {
        "name": "REVERSE",
        "meaning": "previous_direction=-1; Reverse commanded"
      }
    ],
    "transitions": [
      {
        "from": "STOPPED",
        "condition": "Stop OR (ForwardButton == ReverseButton)",
        "to": "STOPPED",
        "action": "cmd_direction=0; next_previous_direction=0; outputs neutral"
      },
      {
        "from": "STOPPED",
        "condition": "ForwardButton AND NOT ReverseButton AND NOT Stop",
        "to": "FORWARD",
        "action": "cmd_direction=+1; next_previous_direction=+1; Forward only"
      },
      {
        "from": "STOPPED",
        "condition": "ReverseButton AND NOT ForwardButton AND NOT Stop",
        "to": "REVERSE",
        "action": "cmd_direction=-1; next_previous_direction=-1; Reverse only"
      },
      {
        "from": "FORWARD",
        "condition": "Stop OR (ForwardButton == ReverseButton)",
        "to": "STOPPED",
        "action": "cmd_direction=0; next_previous_direction=0; outputs neutral"
      },
      {
        "from": "FORWARD",
        "condition": "ForwardButton AND NOT ReverseButton AND NOT Stop",
        "to": "FORWARD",
        "action": "cmd_direction=+1; next_previous_direction=+1; Forward only"
      },
      {
        "from": "FORWARD",
        "condition": "ReverseButton AND NOT ForwardButton AND NOT Stop",
        "to": "STOPPED",
        "action": "opposite-direction interlock: cmd_direction=0; next_previous_direction=0; outputs neutral for this scan; next scan may enter REVERSE if request persists"
      },
      {
        "from": "FORWARD",
        "condition": "NOT ForwardButton AND NOT ReverseButton AND NOT Stop",
        "to": "STOPPED",
        "action": "cmd_direction=0; next_previous_direction=0; outputs neutral"
      },
      {
        "from": "REVERSE",
        "condition": "Stop OR (ForwardButton == ReverseButton)",
        "to": "STOPPED",
        "action": "cmd_direction=0; next_previous_direction=0; outputs neutral"
      },
      {
        "from": "REVERSE",
        "condition": "ReverseButton AND NOT ForwardButton AND NOT Stop",
        "to": "REVERSE",
        "action": "cmd_direction=-1; next_previous_direction=-1; Reverse only"
      },
      {
        "from": "REVERSE",
        "condition": "ForwardButton AND NOT ReverseButton AND NOT Stop",
        "to": "STOPPED",
        "action": "opposite-direction interlock: cmd_direction=0; next_previous_direction=0; outputs neutral for this scan; next scan may enter FORWARD if request persists"
      },
      {
        "from": "REVERSE",
        "condition": "NOT ForwardButton AND NOT ReverseButton AND NOT Stop",
        "to": "STOPPED",
        "action": "cmd_direction=0; next_previous_direction=0; outputs neutral"
      }
    ]
  },
  "timer_plan": {
    "required": false,
    "timers": [],
    "PT_durations": "N/A; no TON/TOF/RTO used. The required one-scan neutral is implemented by state-transition memory, not by a timer.",
    "reset_conditions": "On instance reset/initial scan: previous_direction:=0, qForward:=FALSE, qReverse:=FALSE, cmd_direction:=0, state:=STOPPED, Forward:=FALSE, Reverse:=FALSE. No timer reset is required because no timer FBs are used."
  },
  "priorities": [
    "1. Safety: Stop=TRUE forces neutral and clears direction memory.",
    "2. Safety: ambiguous input ForwardButton=ReverseButton forces neutral and clears direction memory.",
    "3. Safety interlock: a valid request opposite to the last active direction forces a one-scan neutral output and clears direction memory to 0.",
    "4. Operational: valid single-direction request from neutral or same direction is applied immediately in the same scan.",
    "5. Outputs are mutually exclusive; Forward and Reverse are never TRUE simultaneously.",
    "6. Retained direction memory is updated only from the final commanded direction; reset initializes all memory to stopped/neutral."
  ],
  "initial_values": {
    "state": "STOPPED",
    "previous_direction": 0,
    "cmd_direction": 0,
    "qForward": false,
    "qReverse": false,
    "Forward": false,
    "Reverse": false
  },
  "scan_execution_order": [
    "1. Edge sampling: sample ForwardButton, ReverseButton, and Stop once into the scan snapshot; latch qForward and qReverse from the previous observed outputs and latch previous_direction before any state/output changes. No edge timers are used; inputs are level-sensitive.",
    "2. Safety/reset priority and state transitions: apply reset first; then evaluate Stop and ForwardButton==ReverseButton as highest-priority neutral commands; compute desired direction; if desired is nonzero and opposite to previous_direction, set cmd_direction=0 and transition to STOPPED with next_previous_direction=0 for the one-scan interlock; otherwise set cmd_direction=desired and transition to the corresponding STOPPED/FORWARD/REVERSE state with next_previous_direction=cmd_direction. Commit next state/memory for the next scan, not the current outputs.",
    "3. Unconditional top-level timer FB calls outside CASE/IF: no timer FBs are required for SELF002. If any future timer is added, call every TON/TOF/RTO instance unconditionally at top level outside CASE/IF with fixed PT and explicit reset conditions.",
    "4. Unified output assignments: in one block, assign Forward := (cmd_direction = +1) AND NOT reset; Reverse := (cmd_direction = -1) AND NOT reset; then store qForward := Forward and qReverse := Reverse for the next scan. No other writes to Forward or Reverse are permitted."
  ],
  "formal_assertions": [
    {
      "id": "A1",
      "formula": "G(!(Forward & Reverse))"
    },
    {
      "id": "A2",
      "formula": "G((Stop | (ForwardButton <-> ReverseButton)) -> (!Forward & !Reverse))"
    },
    {
      "id": "A3",
      "formula": "G((Reverse & X(ForwardButton & !ReverseButton & !Stop)) -> X(!Forward & !Reverse))"
    },
    {
      "id": "A4",
      "formula": "G((Forward & X(ReverseButton & !ForwardButton & !Stop)) -> X(!Forward & !Reverse))"
    }
  ]
}

CODESYS DIALECT CARDS:
[
  {
    "id": "ton_timer",
    "title": "Standard IEC TON Timer Block Invocation",
    "body": "// Standard IEC TON timer: MUST invoke unconditionally OUTSIDE CASE/IF every scan!\nVAR\n    timer : TON;\n    runTimer : BOOL;\nEND_VAR\n// Control via boolean IN flag (never put timer(...) only inside an IF/CASE arm):\nrunTimer := (state = 1) AND NOT resetCmd;\ntimer(IN := runTimer, PT := T#2s);\nIF timer.Q THEN\n    // Timer expired; timer.ET holds elapsed time\nEND_IF;"
  }
]
